They resemble snakes, worms, and scorpions; among them are the yellow plum (zardālu), the asrad, and the baza,
in degree, with its varieties and differences; their leaves resemble those of the mughras tree; they are cold and sticky.
Among the creatures: Come, O Commander of the Faithful, 'Ali, peace be upon him, the Messenger of God, peace be upon him, said:
"The dearest of prophets to God Almighty is he whom the believers love, and God has for them a covenant."
Every year it comes to the Prophet on that day, and they say: "If you are truthful,
call upon God Almighty so that He may ward off from us this misfortune of Elias upon us in this color."
The plants and their followers were as if yellowed; the Prophet summoned them, they came, were purified and elevated,
and the sun, from every quarter over each place, great wonders appeared, and its sweet fruits
over each great place, not one day passes without its warmth purifying it; the yellow plum benefits women and relieves
thirst; and the cause of bloodiness and bitterness goes away from these; it is attributed to relieving toothache,
it settles the teeth; fresh shoots bring it, it kills lice, it reduces fever in the belly;
it calms the stomach and intestines, prevents putrefaction and corruption of bile, relieves pain and sharpens the mind;
it destroys worms and dryness; its stone, used as medicine, expels bladder stones and is beneficial for the water;
it is beneficial; its stone relieves pain; the people of India and Egypt use it; it relieves pain in the body;
if one fears nightblindness and does not find a remedy in Isfahan, let him seek Mary's herb; it is suitable;
whoever turns away his nightblindness and does not feed it will not find it pleasant; it is from ancient times;
bread and milk with fenugreek should be its food, you will find it; its water cures the liver and is good for it;
it is beneficial for the stomach, strengthening; it increases power, gives water, and opens;
it prevents vomiting; [Nārjabil] — ginger from India — is sought for the pilgrimage; it is good.
One degree: in small amounts, it is the way of the pure; it relieves the body and is a fine remedy;
it purifies the interior with a warm, gentle, and fine quality, cleanses within, and benefits the constitution.

